Status/Updates:</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 3.4 M1 has been through QA =
pending release approval with two QA issues =
highlighted.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 3.1.9 is being built ready =
for QA.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Big thanks to Paul Gortmaker =
for tracking down the cause of an LTP null pointer dereference (and =
other errors) within the cgroups mount code which was responsible for =
several of our LTP hangs. The issue was introduced in new code between =
5.0 and 5.1 in the kernel and had been present for a while. The fix is =
now making its way through various kernel trees =
upstream.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Sadly, the above fix did not =
resolve the &#8220;rcu&#8221; autobuilder VM hangs we are seeing =
occasionally. These are odd in that they affect kvm and non-kvm builds =
(x86 and arm seen on x86-64 hosts), they pin the VM at 300-400% CPU =
usage and the VM will respond to pings but no ssh or console output. The =
rcu dumps from the kernel are likely a symptom that something is wrong =
rather than the cause and often look incomplete. It is as if some =
instantaneous host load breaks timers in a way the guest cannot recover =
or continue execution from. We&#8217;re continuing to try and narrow =
this down but it is proving elusive and progress is slow, any insight =
anyone may have would be welcome.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There are new manual sections =
that have recently been added on <a =
href=3D"http://docs.yoctoproject.org/test-manual/reproducible-builds.html=
"><span style=3D'color:#1155CC'>Reproducible Builds</span></a> and <a =
href=3D"http://docs.yoctoproject.org/test-manual/yocto-project-compatible=
.html"><span style=3D'color:#1155CC'>Yocto Project =
Compatible</span></a>.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We continue to deal with an =
issue with centos8 kernels having what looks like bad bounds checking on =
the utimensat_time64 32 bit syscalls where the syscall was backported =
into a kernel point release. We&#8217;re working on reporting it =
upstream.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We have a 10th anniversary =
T-shirt and some other Yocto Project items (hoody, stickers, mugs etc.) =
now available at <a href=3D"https://yoctoproject.org/shop"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://yoctoproject.org/shop</span></a> (EU and =
Americas sources)<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The multiconfig changes in =
bitbake continue to cause problems, we still need simpler test cases to =
reproduce issues rather than huge builds. The existing patches seem to =
fix some workloads and break others. Richard is trying to fix but trying =
to fix autobuilder issues and other problems and these are slow builds =
to debug.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l3 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Intermittent autobuilder issues =
continue to occur and continue to be at record high levels. You can see =
the list of failures we&#8217;re continuing to see by searching for the =
&#8220;AB-INT&#8221; tag in bugzilla: <a =
href=3D"https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-IN=
T"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?qui=
cksearch=3DAB-INT</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
style=3D'mso-margin-top-alt:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin=
-left:.5in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>We are working to =
identify the load pattern on the infrastructure that seems to trigger =
these.</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p =
style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Ways to =
